  {
    "sha": "6a82e57e927e867038fd22f9da4e1770a6e0a2af",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDZhODJlNTdlOTI3ZTg2NzAzOGZkMjJmOWRhNGUxNzcwYTZlMGEyYWY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T14:57:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T14:57:54Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning)!: part off with the whole kerf behind the part's end face\n\nThe Part operation used its parting plane (Bottom Z) as the blade's\ncentre line. With the #641 corner shift a 3 mm blade on orientation 2\nposted Z-71.5 for an end face at Z-70: the kerf Z-71.5..-68.5 took\n1.5 mm and the back chamfer off the finished part, and no check saw it.\n\n- motion: the plane is the finished part's end face. The whole kerf\n  stands on the waste side, derived from the model and the setup stock\n  (parting_law::waste_side). The CL is half a blade from the plane.\n- motion: \"nothing to part\" judges the kerf against the bar (the model\n  widened by the stock's two ends), names the kerf and bar Z spans, and\n  accepts the correct kerf past the part's end. StockEnv gets s_bot.\n- motion/app: part_kerf_refusal refuses at generation a part-off path\n  whose blade band takes finished-part material by more than 1 um.\n- tests: turning_part_kerf (motion), lathe_part_off_kerf (app); pins in\n  lathe_blade_corner, lathe_post, catalog_groove_part_off, turning_blade\n  and the motion turning_blade suite updated; groove_part goldens (mm,\n  inch) and the groove-part-off and cone-thread catalog cases\n  regenerated by their own tools.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the posted Z of every existing part-off moves by half\na blade width toward the bar. Example: end face Z-70, 3 mm blade,\norientation 2: old G01 X0 Z-71.5, new G01 X0 Z-73. A part-off whose kerf\nmeets no known bar (no stock set, plane at the model's end) is now\nrefused by name.\n\nFixes #3452\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
