      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T15:30:36Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): refuse a part-off in a setup that holds the part end for end\n\nSecond re-read of PR #3472: the setup's part alignment is baked into the\nfacets, so in an OP20 flip setup the chuck at -Z holds the FINISHED part\nand the free end is scrap. The chuck-side rule then put the kerf of a\nstubbed model (Z-84..0 flipped, plane Z-14) at Z-17..-14, 3 mm into the\npart, and the verdict, which reads the same side, was silent.\n\n- app: collect_job refuses a Part op when setup_align::reverses_axis\n  holds (the alignment turns document +Z to a negative setup Z - any\n  axis reversal, not only the flip preset), by name, in plain English.\n- motion: CHUCK_NOTE is plain words and goes on the path only where the\n  rule decides what is kept (model on both sides of the plane,\n  parting_law::rule_decides); the refusals say \"lower Z\", not \"-Z\".\n- tests: lathe_part_off_kerf gains the flipped setup (stubbed and\n  part-only models, both refused) and the stubbed pin held as modelled\n  (posts Z-73); turning_part_kerf pins where the note appears. The\n  catalog .camproj files drop the note again (their planes are at the\n  model's end).\n\nFixes #3452\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
